</table>
</span></div>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 1: </span>Performance on MGSM and MSVAMP.
Bn/Th/Sw are mid<span id="S1.T1.10" class="ltx_text">-</span>resource (MRL); the other seven languages are high<span id="S1.T1.11" class="ltx_text">-</span>resource (HRL).
Sub<span id="S1.T1.12" class="ltx_text">-</span>headings (e.g. “Metamath<span id="S1.T1.13" class="ltx_text">-</span>7B &amp; mT5<span id="S1.T1.14" class="ltx_text">-</span>XL”) specify the <em id="S1.T1.15" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">decoder base model</em> and the <em id="S1.T1.16" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">multilingual encoder</em>.
LangBridge, MindMerger, and MERLIN use both components; SLAM and QAlign adopt only the listed decoder.
<math id="S1.T1.m59" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta</annotation></semantics></math> rows show MERLIN’s absolute gain over MindMerger (<math id="S1.T1.m60" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathord{+}x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>+</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathord{+}x</annotation></semantics></math> for improvements, <math id="S1.T1.m61" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathord{-}x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>-</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathord{-}x</annotation></semantics></math> for drops).</figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="S2" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">2 </span>Methodology</h2>

<div id="S2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Given a lightweight connector that learns to map multilingual encoder states into the English-centric large language model embedding space, MERLIN’s primary goal is to improve representational alignment between the encoder and the LLM within the model-stacking architecture, thereby enabling the LLM to more effectively leverage the rich multilingual features provided by the encoder. This is accomplished through a two-stage process. In the first stage, <span id="S2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Model Stacking</span>—multilingual parallel data is leveraged to enhance the mapping capabilities of the connector module, also referred to as the mapping layer. This component is responsible for projecting the encoder’s multilingual representations into the LLM’s embedding space. In the second stage, <span id="S2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Task Specialization</span>—the focus shifts to the LLM itself. Here, a rank-constrained adaptation (e.g., DoRA<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib25" title="" class="ltx_ref">Liu et al., 2024</a>)</cite>) is applied, tuning a small set of parameters to enable the decoder to reason effectively over the enriched cross-lingual input, conditioned on both the encoder outputs and the Mapping Layer. This approach not only enhances the mapping capability of the connector module but also enables the LLM to adaptively utilize the rich multilingual representations during the task-solving process. The following sections detail the objectives and data used in each stage.</p>
</div>
<section id="S2.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">2.1 </span>Stage I: Model stacking Stage</h3>

<div id="S2.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Stage I is designed to help the decoder learn to interpret encoder representations without modifying its original parameters. This is accomplished through a three-step curriculum that gradually improves cross-lingual alignment, laying the groundwork for the subsequent task specialization stage, where the model’s reasoning capabilities are further refined.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Problem Definition: </span>Let <math id="S2.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q</annotation></semantics></math> be a target-language sentence of length <math id="S2.SS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell</annotation></semantics></math>.
A pretrained multilingual encoder produces <math id="S2.SS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X=\operatorname{Enc}(q)\in\mathbb{R}^{\ell\times d_{\text{enc}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>Enc</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mtext>enc</mtext></msub></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X=\operatorname{Enc}(q)\in\mathbb{R}^{\ell\times d_{\text{enc}}}</annotation></semantics></math>. A two-layer perceptron
<math id="S2.SS1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{\sigma}:\mathbb{R}^{d_{\text{enc}}}\!\rightarrow\!\mathbb{R}^{d_{\text{llm}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>σ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><msub><mi>d</mi><mtext>enc</mtext></msub></msup><mo rspace="0.108em" stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><msub><mi>d</mi><mtext>llm</mtext></msub></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{\sigma}:\mathbb{R}^{d_{\text{enc}}}\!\rightarrow\!\mathbb{R}^{d_{\text{llm}}}</annotation></semantics></math>, with parameters
<math id="S2.SS1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>σ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma</annotation></semantics></math>, projects these states into the LLM space, <math id="S2.SS1.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{f}=f_{\sigma}(X)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>σ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{f}=f_{\sigma}(X)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">The model stacking stage is divided into three consecutive sub-stages that progressively specialize the connector while the encoder and the LLM remain frozen.</p>
</div>
<section id="S2.SS1.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">(a) General bilingual mapping (Map.)</h4>

<div id="S2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">An initial bridge is established with a generic bitext from <math id="S2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{\text{tgt}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>L</mi><mtext>tgt</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{\text{tgt}}</annotation></semantics></math>, a generic sentence in the target language, to English <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib19" title="" class="ltx_ref">Huang et al., 2024</a>)</cite>. The
decoder receives only the projected encoder states</p>
<table id="S2.Ex1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{\sigma}(q)=\bigl[\langle\texttt{bos}\rangle;\,X_{f};\,\langle\texttt{sep}\rangle\bigr]," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>σ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">bos</mtext><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.337em">;</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.337em">;</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">sep</mtext><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{\sigma}(q)=\bigl[\langle\texttt{bos}\rangle;\,X_{f};\,\langle\texttt{sep}\rangle\bigr],</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">and the connector parameters are obtained from</p>
<table id="S2.Ex2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma^{(1)}=\arg\!\min_{\sigma}\mathbb{E}_{(\tilde{s},s^{\star})}\!\bigl[-\log p_{\text{LLM}}\!\bigl(s^{\star}\mid M_{\sigma}(\tilde{s})\bigr)\bigr]," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo>⁡</mo><munder><mi>min</mi><mi>σ</mi></munder></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>s</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">−</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mtext>LLM</mtext></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>σ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>s</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma^{(1)}=\arg\!\min_{\sigma}\mathbb{E}_{(\tilde{s},s^{\star})}\!\bigl[-\log p_{\text{LLM}}\!\bigl(s^{\star}\mid M_{\sigma}(\tilde{s})\bigr)\bigr],</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.3" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>s</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{s}</annotation></semantics></math> is the target-language sentence and <math id="S2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s^{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s^{\star}</annotation></semantics></math> its English reference. The loss
encourages <math id="S2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{\sigma}(\tilde{s})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>σ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>s</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{\sigma}(\tilde{s})</annotation></semantics></math> to be a close representation of <math id="S2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s^{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s^{\star}</annotation></semantics></math> in the LLM space.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S2.SS1.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">(b) Question Alignment (Align.)</h4>

<div id="S2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The connector is then refined with translated prompts
<math id="S2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\tilde{q},q^{\star})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>q</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\tilde{q},q^{\star})</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="S2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{q}</annotation></semantics></math> is a
question in <math id="S2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{\text{tgt}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>L</mi><mtext>tgt</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{\text{tgt}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q^{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>q</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q^{\star}</annotation></semantics></math> is its English counterpart:</p>
<table id="S2.Ex3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma^{(2)}=\arg\!\min_{\sigma}\mathbb{E}_{(\tilde{q},q^{\star})}\!\bigl[-\log p_{\text{LLM}}\!\bigl(q^{\star}\mid M_{\sigma}(\tilde{q})\bigr)\bigr]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo>⁡</mo><munder><mi>min</mi><mi>σ</mi></munder></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>q</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">−</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mtext>LLM</mtext></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msup><mi>q</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>σ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma^{(2)}=\arg\!\min_{\sigma}\mathbb{E}_{(\tilde{q},q^{\star})}\!\bigl[-\log p_{\text{LLM}}\!\bigl(q^{\star}\mid M_{\sigma}(\tilde{q})\bigr)\bigr].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">This step encourages the representations of non-English prompts to align closely with the semantic space utilized by the LLM for English reasoning.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S2.SS1.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">(c) Task-aware Augmentation (Aug.)</h4>

<div id="S2.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Finally, translated question–answer pairs <math id="S2.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\tilde{q},a^{\star})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\tilde{q},a^{\star})</annotation></semantics></math> inject task-specific supervision.
Here the decoder is allowed to see both the encoder projection and its own token embeddings
<math id="S2.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T(q)=E_{\text{LLM}}[q]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>E</mi><mtext>LLM</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T(q)=E_{\text{LLM}}[q]</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="S2.Ex4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(X_{f},T)(q)=\bigl[\langle\texttt{bos}\rangle;\,X_{f};\,\langle\texttt{sep}\rangle;\,T(q)\bigr]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">bos</mtext><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.337em">;</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.337em">;</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">sep</mtext><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.337em">;</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(X_{f},T)(q)=\bigl[\langle\texttt{bos}\rangle;\,X_{f};\,\langle\texttt{sep}\rangle;\,T(q)\bigr].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">The objective becomes</p>
<table id="S2.Ex5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center">
<div id="S2.Ex5.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_markedasmath ltx_transformed_outer" style="width:345.0pt;height:24.1pt;vertical-align:-9.2pt;"><span class="ltx_transformed_inner" style="transform:translate(68.3pt,-4.8pt) scale(1.65564413352169,1.65564413352169) ;">
<p id="S2.Ex5.1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S2.Ex5.m1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma^{(3)}=\arg\!\min_{\sigma}\mathbb{E}_{(\tilde{q},a^{\star})}\!\bigl[-\log p_{\text{LLM}}\!\bigl(a^{\star}\mid(X_{f},T)(\tilde{q})\bigr)\bigr]," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>3</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo>⁡</mo><msub><mi>min</mi><mi>σ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">−</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mtext>LLM</mtext></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma^{(3)}=\arg\!\min_{\sigma}\mathbb{E}_{(\tilde{q},a^{\star})}\!\bigl[-\log p_{\text{LLM}}\!\bigl(a^{\star}\mid(X_{f},T)(\tilde{q})\bigr)\bigr],</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</span></div></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.3" class="ltx_p">yielding the final connector <math id="S2.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma^{\ast}=\sigma^{(3)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>3</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma^{\ast}=\sigma^{(3)}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S2.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">2.2 </span>Stage II: Task Specialization</h3>

<div id="S2.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Stage II internalizes the cross-lingual signal inside the decoder; enhances the integration of multilingual representations within the decoder and plays a critical role in improving performance on complex reasoning tasks. The connector
<math id="S2.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma^{\ast}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>σ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma^{\ast}</annotation></semantics></math>, the encoder and all pretrained LLM weights remain fixed; only rank-constrained DoRA <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib25" title="" class="ltx_ref">Liu et al., 2024</a>)</cite>
matrices <math id="S2.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>θ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta</annotation></semantics></math> inside the decoder are activated.
For every English task example <math id="S2.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(q,a^{\star})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(q,a^{\star})</annotation></semantics></math> the input takes the augmented form <math id="S2.SS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(X_{f},T)(q)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(X_{f},T)(q)</annotation></semantics></math>
defined above. The adaptation parameters are obtained through</p>
<table id="S2.Ex6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center">
<div id="S2.Ex6.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_markedasmath ltx_transformed_outer" style="width:345.0pt;height:21.6pt;vertical-align:-6.2pt;"><span class="ltx_transformed_inner" style="transform:translate(71.5pt,-4.5pt) scale(1.70869819635347,1.70869819635347) ;">
<p id="S2.Ex6.1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S2.Ex6.m1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta^{\ast}=\arg\!\min_{\theta}\mathbb{E}_{(q,a^{\star})}\!\bigl[-\log p_{\text{LLM}_{\theta}}\!\bigl(a^{\star}\mid(X_{f},T)(q)\bigr)\bigr]." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo>⁡</mo><msub><mi>min</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">−</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><msub><mtext>LLM</mtext><mi>θ</mi></msub></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta^{\ast}=\arg\!\min_{\theta}\mathbb{E}_{(q,a^{\star})}\!\bigl[-\log p_{\text{LLM}_{\theta}}\!\bigl(a^{\star}\mid(X_{f},T)(q)\bigr)\bigr].</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</span></div></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">DoRA constrains learning to a negligible fraction of the total parameter count while letting the model
gradually absorb how to exploit <math id="S2.SS2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{f}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{f}</annotation></semantics></math> during generation.</p>
</div>
<section id="S2.SS2.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Inference.</h4>

<div id="S2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Given a target-language query <math id="S2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q</annotation></semantics></math>, the encoder produces <math id="S2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math>, the connector adds the prefix
<math id="S2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{f}=f_{\sigma^{\ast}}(X)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><msup><mi>σ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{f}=f_{\sigma^{\ast}}(X)</annotation></semantics></math>, and the adapted decoder <math id="S2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{LLM}_{\theta^{\ast}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>LLM</mi><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{LLM}_{\theta^{\ast}}</annotation></semantics></math> generates
the answer in English from <math id="S2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(X_{f},T)(q)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(X_{f},T)(q)</annotation></semantics></math> <em id="S2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">zero-shot</em> with respect to <math id="S2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{\text{tgt}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>L</mi><mtext>tgt</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{\text{tgt}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S2.T2" class="ltx_table">
<div id="S2.T2.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_center ltx_transformed_outer" style="width:345.0pt;height:120.3pt;vertical-align:-58.9pt;"><span class="ltx_transformed_inner" style="transform:translate(-175.2pt,61.1pt) scale(0.496144596137857,0.496144596137857) ;">
<table id="S2.T2.2.1" class="ltx_tabular ltx_align_middle">
<tr id="S2.T2.2.1.1" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S2.T2.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_tt" style="padding-left:4.0pt;padding-right:4.0pt;"><span id="S2.T2.2.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Model</span></td>
<td id="S2.T2.2.1.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_tt" style="padding-left:4.0pt;padding-right:4.0pt;"><span id="S2.T2.2.1.1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">amh</span></td>
<td id="S2.T2.2.1.1.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_tt" style="padding-left:4.0pt;padding-right:4.0pt;"><span id="S2.T2.2.1.1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">ewe</span></td>
<td id="S2.T2.2.1.1.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_tt" style="padding-left:4.0pt;padding-right:4.0pt;"><span id="S2.T2.2.1.1.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">hau</span></td>
<td id="S2.T2.2.1.1.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_tt" style="padding-left:4.0pt;padding-right:4.0pt;"><span id="S2.T2.2.1.1.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">ibo</span></td>
<td id="S2.T2.2.1.1.6" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_tt" style="padding-left:4.0pt;padding-right:4.0pt;"><span id="S2.T2.2.1.1.6.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">kin</span></td>
<td id="S2.T2.2.1.1.7" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_tt" style="padding-left:4.0pt;padding-right:4.0pt;"><span id="S2.T2.2.1.1.7.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">lin</span></td>
<td id="S2.T2.2.1.1.8" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_tt" style="padding-left:4.0pt;padding-right:4.0pt;"><span id="S2.T2.2.1.1.8.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">lug</span></td>
<td id="S2.T2.2.1.1.9" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_tt" style="padding-left:4.0pt;padding-right:4.0pt;"><span id="S2.T2.2.1.1.9.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">orm</span></td>
<td id="S2.T2.2.1.1.10" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_tt" style="padding-left:4.0pt;padding-right:4.0pt;"><span id="S2.T2.2.1.1.10.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">sna</span></td>
<td id="S2.T2.2.1.1.11" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_tt" style="padding-left:4.0pt;padding-right:4.0pt;"><span id="S2.T2.2.1.1.11.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">sot</span></td>
